{"id": "sevt_014yQkg5ATkUjK1QA6TLX4oJ", "content": [{"text": "**Cause:** the checkout deploy `07000f4` brought back the N+1 query pattern. The rolled-back `510eca7` didn't cause the spike.\n\n**Deploys (last 6h):**\n- `07000f4` (checkout, 14:08:45) is the \"readability refactor\". p99 climbs from about 77ms to 110ms at 14:08, then rises steadily to about 423ms by 14:29.\n- `510eca7` (checkout, 14:26) was rolled back at 14:29:10. It only changed a log line in the middleware, so it can't affect latency. It is a red herring.\n- The auth deploy at 11:30 is too early to line up.\n\n**Diff of `07000f4`:** it replaces one batched `order_id IN (...)` query and an in-memory grouping with a loop that runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=...)` once per open order. That is a per-row query where there used to be a batch.\n\n**Metrics and logs:**\n- `db_pool_utilization` for checkout rises in step from 0.13 at 14:08 to 0.70 at 14:29, and reaches 1.0 at 14:39 and stays there.\n- p99 jumps from 423ms to 3849ms at 14:30, one minute after the rollback, so the rollback didn't cause it either. It stays around 4\u20135s after that. I did not find the exact trigger for the 14:30 step.\n- `app.log` shows the new per-order `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` queries starting at 14:08:57 on checkout-1. They run at 6 to 180 per minute from 14:08 to 14:59.\n- I did not check auth, cart or inventory pool utilization, or upstream dependencies.\n\n**Suggested action:** revert `07000f4` and restore the batched query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `07000f4` \u2014 the refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with one query per order, which grew checkout's DB pool use from about 13% to 100% and drove up p99.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:53:56.630413Z", "type": "agent.message"}
